mc.respond's How To by bassin247 - Michael Kennedy <bassin247@eggheads.org>


How to use bot
here are the basic commands...


1)
to add a topic for use on all channels with a 1 line msg reply

(@pimpin): bot-, add all testing /msg %chan testing this shit
(@bot-): Ok pimpin, set.
(@pimpin): testing
(@bot-): testing this shit

2)
to add a topic for use on 1 channel with a 1 line msg reply

(@pimpin): bot-, add #pureISO testing /msg %chan testing this shit
(@bot-): Ok pimpin, set.
(@pimpin): testing
(@bot-): testing this shit
the only difference between 1 and 2 is bot- will only reply to testing in #pureISO, in step one he will respond to testing in any channel

3)
to add a topic for use on all channels with a 1 line action reply

(@pimpin): bot-, add all testing /action %chan tests this shit
(@bot-): Ok pimpin, set.
(@pimpin): testing
* bot- tests this shit

4)
to add a topic for use on all channels with a multiple line msg reply

(@pimpin): bot-, add all testing /msg %chan testing -AND- /msg %chan testing1,2 -AND- /msg %chan testing1,2,3
(@bot-): Ok pimpin, set.
(@pimpin): testing
(@bot-): testing
(@bot-): testing1,2
(@bot-): testing1,2,3

5)
to add a topic for use on all channels with a multiple line msg and action reply

(@pimpin): bot-, add all testing /msg %chan testing -AND- /action %chan tests this shit once -AND- /action %chan tests this shit twice -AND- /msg %chan this shit mist work
(@bot-): Ok pimpin, set.
(@pimpin): testing
(@bot-): testing
* bot- tests this shit once
* bot- tests this shit twice
(@bot-): this shit mist work

6)
to delete a topic "testing" thats used on all channels

(@pimpin): bot-, del all testing
(@bot-): Ok pimpin, set.

7)
to delete a topic "testing" thats used on a single channel

(@pimpin): bot-, del #pureISO testing
(@bot-): Ok pimpin, set.

8)
to search bot-'s database
bot-, search word
1 match (out of 129 entries) found for word; all word

9)
to get the info for a particular topic in bot-'s database.
(@pimpin): bot-, info all testing
(@bot-): pimpin: all testing /msg %chan random test response 1

10)
to add a random response to the bot-

[22:32] (@pimpin): bot-, add all testing /msg %chan random test response 1
[22:32] (@bot-): Ok pimpin, set.
[22:32] (@pimpin): bot-, addor all testing /msg %chan random test response 2
[22:32] (@bot-): Ok pimpin, set.
[22:32] (@pimpin): testing
[22:32] (@bot-): random test response 2
[22:32] (@pimpin): testing
[22:32] (@bot-): random test response 1

11)
to delete a random response from bot-

first the information
(@pimpin) bot-, search testing
(@bot-) 1 match (out of 129 entries) found for testing; all testing
(@pimpin) bot-, info all testing
(@bot-): pimpin: all testing /msg %chan random test response 1 -OR- /msg %chan random test response 2

now the syntax
(@pimpin): bot-, delor 2 all testing
(@bot-): Ok pimpin, set.
what I did was deleted the second reply hence the 2

the info now is this..
(@pimpin): bot-, info all testing
(@bot-): pimpin: all testing /msg %chan random test response 1

12)
seaching bot-'s replies for particular words
(@pimpin): bot-, dsearch fuck
(@bot-): 6 matches (out of 129 entries) found for fuck; #cablemodemwarez *I+will+give*leech* all fuck all errr* #cablemodemwarez *big+reward* all shut+up+%botnick all go+fuck+yourself+%botnick

13)
variables..
%chan == the #channel's name
%nick == the nick of the user
%botnick == the bot's nickname

14)
making bot- kick people
use as the response..
/quote kick %chan %nick :kick reason.

15)
making bot respond to an action in #channel
?ACTION+kicks+%botnick? would have bot- reply to /me kicks bot-